.Dd June 26, 2026
.Dt VSAPMINFO 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vsapminfo
.Nd determines information about an Apple Partition Map (APM) volume system
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm vsapminfo
.Op Fl b Ar bytes_per_sector
.Op Fl hvV
.Ar source
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm vsapminfo
is a utility to determine information about an Apple Partition Map (APM) \
volume system
.Pp
.Nm vsapminfo
is part of the
.Nm libvsapm
package.
.Nm libvsapm
is a library to access the Apple Partition Map (APM) volume system format
.Pp
.Ar source
is the source image.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl b Ar bytes_per_sector
specify the number of bytes per sector (default is 512).
Use this to override the automatic bytes per sector detection
.It Fl h
shows this help
.It Fl v
verbose output to stderr
.It Fl V
print version
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
None
.Sh FILES
None
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
# vsapminfo /dev/sda
vsapminfo 20260626
.sp
Apple Partition Map (APM) information:
	Bytes per sector	: 512
	Number of partitions	: 2
.sp
Partition: 1
	Type			: Apple_HFS
	Name			: Foo
	Offset			: 33792 (0x00008400)
	Size			: 228352
	Status flags		: 0x0000007f
		Is valid
		Is allocated
		Is in use
		Contains boot information
		Is readable
		Is writeable
		Boot code is position independent
.sp
Partition: 2
	Type			: Apple_Free
	Name			: Extra
	Offset			: 32768 (0x00008000)
	Size			: 1024
	Status flags		: 0x00000000
.sp
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
Errors, verbose and debug output are printed to stderr when verbose output \
\-v is enabled.
Verbose and debug output are only printed when enabled at compilation.
